---
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const title = "Atpiano privacy note";
const description =
  "How Atpiano handles email addresses submitted to the hosted-access interest list.";
---

<SiteLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/privacy/">
  <SiteHeader />
  <main class="prose-page">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>A small list with a narrow purpose.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        If you join the hosted Atpiano interest list, your email address is used
        only to learn whether people want a browser-based version and to contact
        you if hosted Atpiano becomes available.
      </p>

      <h2>What is stored</h2>
      <p>
        The list stores your email address, the time you joined, the page where
        you joined, and the version of this consent notice. Duplicate signups
        update the existing entry rather than creating additional records.
      </p>

      <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
      <p>
        The marketing site and signup database run on Cloudflare. Cloudflare
        Turnstile is used to distinguish ordinary visitors from automated form
        submissions. The Atpiano list does not intentionally retain your IP
        address or browser fingerprint.
      </p>

      <h2>What it is not used for</h2>
      <p>
        Joining this list does not create an Atpiano account. The address is not
        sold, shared for unrelated marketing, or added to a general newsletter.
      </p>

      <h2>Removal and questions</h2>
      <p>
        To ask what is stored or to have your address removed, email
        <a href="mailto:kyle@graehlarts.com?subject=Atpiano%20privacy"
        >kyle@graehlarts.com</a>. Future list emails will also provide a simple
        way to opt out.
      </p>

      <p>Last updated: August 25, 2026.</p>
      <p><a href="/">← Return to the Atpiano homepage</a></p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</SiteLayout>
